<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-3">3 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Teatro Olimpico opens in Vicenza</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-palladio">Andrea Palladio</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> opened with a performance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophocles">Sophocles</a>'s '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oedipus">Oedipus</a> Rex'. Its permanent painted street scenes survive, making it the oldest surviving enclosed theatre in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/composition-of-connacht">Composition of Connacht</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Composition of Connacht was a settlement of 1585 between the English government under the lord deputy Sir John Perrot and the lords of Connacht and Thomond.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nonsuch">Treaty of Nonsuch</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Nonsuch was signed on 10 August 1585 at Nonsuch Palace in Surrey between Elizabeth I of England and the Dutch rebels.</p></div></li></ol></section>
